course: dictionary
lesson: 10404
title: Trickle and slow movement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a thing). Trickle works both ways. «Sand trickling through a glass» shows the action: the sand moves slowly, in a thin stream. «A trickle of water» uses trickle as a noun, meaning a thin, slow flow.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «the ink trickling down his face», the word down and the word face tell you the ink moves slowly, in thin drops, not in a gush. Trickle always means slow and small, never fast or big.
explain: Trickle can also be about people. «Fans trickle in» means they arrive slowly, a few at a time, not all at once. To check, swap in your meaning: «Fans arrive slowly, a few at a time» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Trickle is a verb and a noun: you can trickle, or you can see a trickle.
fact: «Trickling» means flowing slowly in a thin line or in small drops.
fact: «A trickle» means a thin, slow flow of liquid, or a small number of people or things arriving slowly.
fact: «Trickle in» and «trickle out» mean people arrive or leave slowly, a few at a time.
fact: In science, water trickling through soil or rock is slow, and a stream can shrink to a trickle in summer.
exercise: «Bill uses the ink trickling down his face to write again.» What is the ink doing? | Flying up into the air | *Flowing slowly in a thin line | Splashing loudly into a bowl | Freezing solid on his skin
exercise: What does «a trickle of water» mean? | *A thin, slow flow of water | A hard, frozen lump of ice | A loud crash of waves | A huge, rushing flood
exercise: «Fans trickle in before the match starts.» What does trickle in mean? | *Arrive slowly, a few at a time | Leave all at once with a bang | Sing loudly together | Fall from the sky in a storm
test: In summer the stream is only a trickle. What does this suggest? | Water that is hot like soup | A flood of water rushing over the rocks | *Very little water flowing slowly | Water that has frozen solid
test: «A trickle of blood ran down her arm.» Which word is a noun in this sentence? | down | ran | arm | *trickle
exam: Dev says a trickle is a big, fast flood. What does trickle really mean? | *A thin, slow flow | A sudden burst of rain | A loud, splashing wave | A big, fast flood
